# Deployment settings for Skrongle mini.
#
#   cp deploy/deploy.env.example deploy/deploy.env     # deploy.env is gitignored
#   $EDITOR deploy/deploy.env
#   scripts/deploy-all.sh                               # deploys to every target configured below
#   scripts/deploy-all.sh pi                            # or name the target
#
# Any setting may instead be exported from your shell (export PI_HOST=... in
# ~/.zshrc); a variable set in the environment overrides the same one here.
#
# Every value here is read by scripts/deploy-all.sh and
# scripts/release.sh (the Pi). Lines starting with # are comments; values with
# spaces need quotes. Nothing in this file is ever sent to the app's users.
#
# This file holds how to reach the target (host, key path). Keep it out of
# version control anyway: it is listed in .gitignore. The *.example file is safe
# to commit because it holds only placeholders and paths.

# =====================================================================
# Which targets scripts/deploy-all.sh deploys to when run without arguments.
# Space-separated; "pi" is the only target.
# =====================================================================
DEPLOY_TARGETS="pi"

# =====================================================================
# Self-hosted target: the Raspberry Pi / DietPi box.
#
# These four may also be exported from your shell (e.g. in ~/.zshrc) instead
# of set here: a variable set in the environment always wins over this file,
# and scripts/release.sh runs without this file at all. The lines below are
# commented out so a fresh copy of this template does not shadow your shell.
#
# PI_HOST        user@host the deploy scripts ssh to. The user needs passwordless
#                sudo (the default on Raspberry Pi OS and DietPi).
# PI_SSH_KEY     Path to the private key for that host (optional; leave empty to
#                use your ssh config / agent). A path is safe to commit; the key
#                itself must never be in the repo.
# PI_PUBLIC_URL  The public URL the app is reached at, including the path prefix.
#                Used for the health check.
# PI_BASE_PATH   The URL prefix nginx mounts the app under ("/spanish"). Must
#                match the path in PI_PUBLIC_URL.
#
# What the Pi deploy does: cross-compiles for the Pi's CPU, rsyncs the binary
# and data/ to /opt/spanish-learning, installs the systemd unit and the nginx
# snippets (see deploy/*.conf; NGINX_TLS_VHOST="" skips nginx), writes the
# public URL to /etc/spanish-learning/env, restarts, checks /healthz.
# =====================================================================
#PI_HOST=dietpi@pi.local
#PI_SSH_KEY=~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#PI_PUBLIC_URL=https://pi.example.org/spanish
#PI_BASE_PATH=/spanish
